    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0302" n="288" xml:id="pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC
                    Indonesia/7–2148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Consulate General at Batavia</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d211-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-23T12:00:00-04:00">July 23,
                            1948—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>340. Usgoc 122. Dept considers reference
                    controversial matters to SC (last sentence final
                    para Gocus 339 Jul 21) highly undesirable
                    because SC discussion such matters could
                    seriously prejudice success of negotiations before GOC which Dept expects will be renewed on full scale upon Cochran’s
                    arrival Aug 9. Endeavor therefore postpone report to SC until Cochran’s arrival.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d211-f2"/> Scott
                    will arrive Aug 3 with full explanation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d211-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d211-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as telegram 336 to The Hague.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d211-f2" n="2" xml:id="d211-f2-content">
                <p>For two telegrams to the Security Council from the GOC on July 23 and 24, see SC, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">3rd yr., Suppl.</hi> (July), pp. 89, 90. These were
                    reported in telegrams 642, July 25 (Gocus
                    342), and 643, July 25 (Gocus 343), from
                    Batavia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
